00:04:30,000 --> 00:04:36,000
Feel the Wrath.

2
00:09:00,000 --> 00:09:06,000
Wrath of the Titans is a fantasy, adventure, action
film directed by Jonathan Liebesman.

3
00:13:30,000 --> 00:13:36,000
Perseus tries to live a quieter life as a village fisherman while – dangerously weakened by humanity's lack of
devotion – the gods are losing control of the long-imprisoned Titans and their ferocious leader, Kronos.

4
00:18:00,000 --> 00:18:06,000
Perseus, played by Sam Worthington.

5
00:22:30,000 --> 00:22:36,000
Zeus, played by Liam Neeson.

6
00:27:00,000 --> 00:27:06,000
Hades, played by Ralph Fiennes.

7
00:31:30,000 --> 00:31:36,000
Andromeda, played by Rosamund Pike.

8
00:36:00,000 --> 00:36:06,000
Hephaestus, played by Bill Nighy.

9
00:40:30,000 --> 00:40:36,000
Ares, played by Edgar Ramírez.

10
00:45:00,000 --> 00:45:06,000
Wrath of the Titans is a 2012 action fantasy film and a
sequel to the 2010 film Clash of the Titans.

11
00:49:30,000 --> 00:49:36,000
The film stars Sam Worthington, Rosamund Pike, Bill Nighy, Édgar Ramírez, Toby Kebbell, Danny Huston, Ralph Fiennes, and Liam Neeson, with
Jonathan Liebesman directing a screenplay by Dan Mazeau and David Leslie Johnson from a story by them and Greg Berlanti.

12
00:54:00,000 --> 00:54:06,000
Wrath of the Titans takes place a decade after the events of the preceding film as the gods lose control over the imprisoned Titans (thanks to humanity's lack of
prayers which also is draining their immortality) and Perseus is called, this time to rescue his father Zeus, overthrow the Titans, and save mankind.

13
00:58:30,000 --> 00:58:36,000
Talk of a sequel began with the release of Clash of the Titans in March 2010.

14
01:03:00,000 --> 01:03:06,000
Writers Dan Mazeau and David Leslie Johnson were hired in June 2010 and
director Jonathan Liebesman was brought on board in August 2010.

15
01:07:30,000 --> 01:07:36,000
The majority of the casting took place between January and February 2011.

16
01:12:00,000 --> 01:12:06,000
Principal photography began in London in March 2011.

17
01:16:30,000 --> 01:16:36,000
Like its predecessor, the film was converted to 3D in post-production.

18
01:21:00,000 --> 01:21:06,000
Wrath of the Titans was released in 2D and 3D on
March 30, 2012, in the United States.

19
01:25:30,000 --> 01:25:36,000
The film received mostly negative reviews from critics and grossed
$302 million worldwide on a budget of $150 million.

20
01:30:00,000 --> 01:30:06,000
A sequel entitled Revenge of the Titans was planned for a 2013 release, but was
cancelled due to Wrath's underperformance and too few ideas for a script.

21
01:34:30,000 --> 01:34:36,000
The film explores themes of hades, mythology, greek mythology, zeus, god.
